# Modernize Emissions Breakdown Table

Transform the breakdown table into a dynamic, premium component that displays results for the most recent year in the dataset.

## Proposed Changes

### Dashboard

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.html)
- Add an ID to the breakdown table header (e.g., `breakdown-year-title`) to update the year dynamically.
- Update IDs for Scope 1, Scope 2, and Total values to be more specific (e.g., `table-scope1-val`, etc. - actually they already have IDs, I'll just use them).

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.js)
- Update [updateBreakdownTable](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.js#286-295) to:
    - Identify the most recent year from the `trend` data.
    - Display that year in the table header.
    - Update the table cells with values specifically for that year.
    - Add a fallback if no data exists.

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard-dark.css](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard-dark.css)
- Modernize `.data-table` styling:
    - Add horizontal padding to rows.
    - Implement a subtle hover effect on rows.
    - Enhance typography and color contrast for key values.
    - Ensure the "Total" row stands out with a bolder style.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Verify the table header correctly identifies the most recent year (e.g., "2024 Results").
- Confirm the values shown match the totals for that specific year in the trend chart.
- Ensure the table styling looks premium and consistent with the rest of the dashboard.
